    A001["<div class='arg'><b>A001 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>The Fed hikes 25bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Friday's CPI data all but lock in a rate hike this week.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Chairman Warsh's Jackson Hole remarks have raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Current market pricing has raised the cost of disappointing expectations significantly.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A002 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A004 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Incoming data soften materially.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Fed communication turns unexpectedly dovish.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>Q:</b> Beyond next week's meeting, uncertainty around the policy path remains.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>IM:</b> The Fed delivers an additional rate hike in October.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>IM:</b> The Fed delivers an additional rate hike in December.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>ALT:</b> There is a material front end rate decline.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>ALT:</b> There is a sharp twist steepening of the curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A002["<div class='arg'><b>A002 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The Fed's choice at the Sept FOMC is between a hike and risking a large bond spike.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Fed risks a sharp and disorderly UST long end move.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> US 30Y rapidly tests 5.75%.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Treasury buybacks prove futile to stop the UST long end move.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A003 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed does not hike with current pricing.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A003["<div class='arg'><b>A003 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Bond price action, including post Friday's CPI, shows the bond likes orthodoxy.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A004["<div class='arg'><b>A004 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>Friday's twist flattening of the Treasury curve provides further justification for a hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh can point to Friday's twist flattening of the Treasury curve as evidence of tighter policy reinforcing inflation-fighting credibility.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A005["<div class='arg'><b>A005 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh in the presser is more Warsh as at Jackson Hole than Warsh as at the July FOMC.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh's Jackson Hole-style presser is largely to support the bond.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Warsh Jackson Hole speech was more transparent about Warsh's outlook.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The Warsh Jackson Hole speech was more transparent about Warsh's reaction function.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A006["<div class='arg'><b>A006 · PREDICTION</b><div class='core pred'><span>Warsh delivers a hawkish hike.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A005 - PREDICTION</b></span></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Sept FOMC communications lean hawkish.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> The SEP shows 50bps of total hikes in '26.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>P:</b> Warsh says that progress on underlying inflation has been insufficient.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c pred'><span><b>CN:</b> Waller dissents dovishly.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports higher front end rates.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Warsh's hawkish hike supports twist flattening of the UST curve.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The USD is supported.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> Risk is challenged.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> <b>A007 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>ALT:</b> A bigger Bessent #quot;house#quot; is needed for the bond.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A007["<div class='arg'><b>A007 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The hawkish hike supports the author's constructive long end asset swap spread view.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower growth risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Lower inflation risk supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Enhanced Fed credibility supports UST investor confidence.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A008["<div class='arg'><b>A008 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bar for the FOMC to #quot;out-hawk#quot; both expectations as well as other G10 central banks is high.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Part of the puzzle of the dollar being unable to rally amid the recent reacceleration in oil, gas, and refined energy products lies in the broader re-pricing of central banks and curves globally.</span><b>[A]</b></div></div>"]
    A009["<div class='arg'><b>A009 · FORECAST</b><div class='core fc'><span>The USD trades more-or-less sideways into year-end (ex-JPY).</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A008 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A010["<div class='arg'><b>A010 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD outcome is determined by the Fed's ability to #quot;out-hawk#quot; market expectations and other G10 central banks.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c fc'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A009 - FORECAST</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A011 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A011["<div class='arg'><b>A011 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>With evolving expectations, considerable two-way risk remains for the USD at Wednesday's meeting.</span><b>[A]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A012 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A013 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> The dollar depreciates swiftly and significantly.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A015 - VIEW</b></span></div></div>"]
    A012["<div class='arg'><b>A012 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed hikes at least 100bp.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>P:</b> The SEP shows broadening support for additional hikes (relative to the June SEP).</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>P:</b> Growth forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>P:</b> Inflation forecasts are elevated even in the context of further hike guidance.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>P:</b> Chair Warsh himself, intentionally or unintentionally, offers some indication that a more prolonged campaign is necessary to return inflation on the path to 2%.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>Q:</b> Chair Warsh's aversion to forward guidance makes the bullish USD case challenging.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>IM:</b> The bullish USD case sees increased market-implied likelihood that the Fed brings current expectations forward.</span><b>[H]</b></div></div>"]
    A013["<div class='arg'><b>A013 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD softens with dovish or non-committal language from Warsh.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> Markets do not have the patience for anything that sounds like a #quot;one and done#quot; type event under the veil of #quot;no forward guidance#quot;.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c view'><span><b>P:</b> <b>A014 - VIEW</b></span></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> The Fed hikes.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
    A014["<div class='arg'><b>A014 · VIEW</b><div class='core view'><span>The USD falls in tandem with rising back-end yields.</span><b>[H]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Messaging muddles the reaction function further.</span><b>[HY]</b></div><div class='c sup'><span><b>CO:</b> Messaging that muddles the reaction function results in rising back-end yields.</span><b>[HY]</b></div></div>"]
